Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:42:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Try-On: take the waist and hem corrections off the sweatpants

The sweatpants packs are rebuilt from the v2.2 pattern, which has its own
rise and leg length: over the 294 simulated fits the band sits 3-6 cm above
the navel and the hem at 4.5-5.7 % of height (ankle bone 3.9 %). The old
corrections were made for the previous pattern (band 7-10 cm above the navel,
hem about 10 cm too high) and would now squash the new rise. The shorts keep
their waistband correction.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018jPcpWq6gasksWFg8o2kes
